␀␀êYou can train several jumping techniques here. The map is linear, just go to the right, taking all Red flags.␀␀␀x␀Oâÿ/á,␀␀êYour goal is to take 2 Red flags, located at the opposite edges of the map, and then come back to the checkered Finish flag. Hint: the 'Map' button will help you find your way.␀␀␀␀¼␀Oâÿ/á␀␀ ãÿ/á␀␀êYour goal is to take the Red flag and go to the checkered Finish flag.
Use the on-screen buttons to control your bike.␀␀€␀Oâÿ/á4␀␀êThe triangular hill is made of ICE, your bike cannot easily climb its slippery surface (try it!). You will need momentum to get to the other side - just back off and gain more speed before attacking the hill.␀␀␀␀Ü␀Oâÿ/á(␀␀êThis level can be completed by simply holding 'GO' until the bike is airborne. The more adventurous could try performing flips - try 'Left' and 'Right' buttons.␀␀␀␀¬␀Oâÿ/á:␀␀êThis level introduces UPDRAFS - powerful forces, that can make you bike fly! Be careful, use 'Left'/'Right' to avoid hitting your head on the ceiling.

Or, just do nothing and the bike will slowly roll itself straight to the Finish.␀␀␀␀ô␀Oâÿ/á?␀␀êGLUE enables you to ride on vertical surfaces. An easy way to complete this level is to ride slowly on the glue-covered wall, holding 'Stop' all the time and only releasing it for brief moments. Do it slowly, so the glue can keep your bike from falling.␀␀␀BOâÿ/á␀␀êThis level combines jumping and glue. The carefully chosen starting position makes the bike complete the level all by itself.␀␀␀ˆ␀Oâÿ/ál␀␀êMeet the PORTALS - mysterious teleporting devices. There are several routes possible for this level, one of them is:
1. Go through the portal to the right to reach the Red flag
2. Release 'GO', the bike falls though the portal again, rides to the left and enters the second portal
3. Start braking before touching the second Red flag so you can stop completely before falling from the ledge. Go back through the portal - the Finish.␀␀␀␀oOâÿ/áPã! ã␀0 á␀␀ ã␀ !1ƒ""€ã␀Sá ␀ á€#0b #€ã␀Sá ␀ á€#0b $€ã␀Sá ␀ á€#0b %€ã␀Sá ␀ á€#0b &€ã␀Sá ␀ á€#0b '€ã␀Sá ␀ á€#0b (€ã␀Sá ␀ á€#0b )€ã␀Sá ␀ á	€#0b *€ã␀Sá ␀ á
