␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀	␀␀␀␀t␀␀␀␀”␀␀␀␀Ü␀␀␀0␀␀␀`␀␀␀’␀␀␀Ê␀␀␀ð␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Performance Options␀␀␀␀€␀␀␀␀␀␀␀"Bike or die!" has found some MP3music on your console.␀␀␀␀␀$€␀␀␀␀␀␀␀You can enable the music playbackif you accept degraded performance.␀␀␀␀F␀“␀␀␀␀␀É␀␀␀␀␀Best Performance, No Music␀␀␀␀␀Z␀“␀␀␀␀␀É␀␀␀␀␀Enable Music, Low Performance␀␀␀␀n␀“␀␀␀␀␀É␀␀␀␀␀Enable Music, Low Graphics Quality␀␀␀␀E␀Œ␀R␀␀␀␀␀É␀␀␀␀␀Music Options...␀␀␀
␀␀Œ␀(␀␀␀␀␀É␀␀␀␀␀Cancel␀␀The name will be used on the Internet Hall of Fame. You should not change the name or your playing history will be inconsistent.

Submission options:
"Publishing" means your game will be available for replay on the Internet. You should not "publish" if you want to keep your driving style in secret.

"Freestyle" option will enroll your recording in the freestyle competition. This requires publishing so the game can be reviewed and evaluated by the visitors.



Resumed games cannot be submitted to the Hall of Fame. You may want to disable "Auto Save & Resume" in Control Options when playing for the Hall of Fame.␀You may need to define a proxy server depending on your operator/ISP requirements. One indication for such requirement is "Bike or Die" failing to submit your scores even though bike.toyspring.com website is accessible in your palm web browser.
If it happens, see if your web browser settings define a proxy server and set the same server in "Bike or Die".␀Player profiles are useful when multiple users play on the same device.

This works in two areas:
- Players can define their own private configuration settings
- The game is aware of individual players' best times so it can act accordingly when the new record is achieved␀The difference is important because it affects how the best scores are processed - this ensures the game can always remember the best scores for a specific person but still allows you to have different configuration profiles that count as one from the Hall of Fame perspective.␀There are 5 game buttons:
- Forward: push the pedals
- Brake: stop the bike
- Balance left&right: push the bike slightly to maintain balance and help with freestyle tricks
- Flip: allows you to go in the opposite direction.

Use the menu Options/Control to redefine those keys.␀Rules:
- get all checkpoint flags (red)

- finish the race by the checkered flag as soon as possible

- avoid obstacles

On some levels there is no finish flag - just get all red flags to complete the race. Similarly, when there are no red flags you can go to the finish flag immediately.␀Become the best biker in the world and win the eternal fame! On the Internet Hall of Fame you can compare your scores with other "Bike or Die" players. See the current champions on bike.toyspring.com. You can submit your scores using the internet-enabled palm (use the menu "Rec/Submit my best times") or with your web browser (detailed instructions available on site)␀"Disable other keys" deactivates unused application buttons so you won't quit the game by accident.



"Auto Save & Resume" is meant mainly for novice players. If you need more control on saving, disable it and save manually by holding the Pause button or a button assigned to "Save location".



The control groups entitled "On entering a new level" and "On starting the game" can be used to enforce a given zoom level and/or pause the game automatically.

"Keep" means the zoom level remains unchanged from its previous setting.␀Games␀␀␀␀␀␀
